          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em D=2 TQFT
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} topological quantum field theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            2.
          %h2#classification Classification
          %p
            When formulated as an (only) “globally” as 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            on a 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"} category of cobordisms
            (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            for more), then D=2 TQFTs have a comparatively simple classification: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+field+theory"} bulk field theory
            is determined by a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+algebra"} Frobenius algebra
            structure on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
            assigned to the circle (
            %a{:href => "#Abrams96"}> Abrams 96
            ).
          %p
            However, such global D=2 TQFTs with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            do not capture the D=2 TQFTs of most interest in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+quantum+field+theories"} cohomological quantum field theories
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten91"} Witten 91
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"} A-model
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            that participate in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+mirror+symmetry"} homological mirror symmetry
          %p
            These richer D=2 TQFTs are instead local TQFTs in the sense of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended TQFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-functors"} (∞,2)-functors
            on a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,2)-category of cobordisms
            (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            for more), typically on “non-compact” 2-d cobordisms, meaning on those that have non-vanishing outgoing bounary. As such they are now classified by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+objects"} Calabi-Yau objects
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C2%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,2)-category
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie 09, section 4.2
            ). For coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-vector+space"} (∞,2)-vector space
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} A-∞ algebras
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-bimodules"} (∞,1)-bimodules
            between them in the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+chain+complexes"} (∞,1)-category of chain complexes
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TCFT"} TCFT
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Getzler92"} Getzler 92
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Segal99"} Segal 99
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Costello04"} Costello 04
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 09, theorem 4.2.11, theorem 4.2.14
