                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+Chern-Simons+theory"} D=4 Chern-Simons theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#global Global
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            result that global closed D=2 TQFTs with coefficients in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            are equivalent to commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+algebra"} Frobenius algebra
            structures is proven rigorously in
          %ul
            %li#Abrams96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lowell+Abrams"}> Lowell Abrams
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Two-dimensional topological quantum field theories and Frobenius algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 5
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218216596000333"} doi:10.1142/S0218216596000333
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://home.gwu.edu/~labrams/docs/tqft.ps"} ps
          %p The classification result for open-closed D=2 TQFTs was famously announced and sketched in
          %ul
            %li#MooreSegal02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"}> Greg Moore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
                %em Lectures on branes, K-theory and RR charges, Clay Math Institute Lecture Notes (2002),
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.physics.rutgers.edu/~gmoore/clay1/clay1.html"}> web
                )
            %li#Lazaroiu00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calin+Lazaroiu"}> Calin Lazaroiu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the structure of open-closed topological field theory in two dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0010269"} arXiv:hep-th/0010269
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#Kock2004
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"}> Joachim Kock
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Frobenius Algebras and 2d Topological Quantum Field Theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511615443
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.cat/~kock/TQFT.html"} webpage
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.es/~kock/TQFT/FS.pdf"} course notes pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Kock-FrobAlgTQFT-short.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p A picture-rich description of what’s going on:
          %ul
            %li#LaudaPfeiffer05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Lauda"}> Aaron Lauda
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hendryk+Pfeiffer"} Hendryk Pfeiffer
              %em Open-closed strings: two-dimensional extended TQFTs and Frobenius algebras
              , Topology Appl. 155 (2008) 623-666. (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0510664"}> arXiv:math.AT/0510664
              )
          %h3#local Local
          %p
            The local (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"}> extended TQFT
            ) version of D=2 TQFT which captures the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            was mathematically introduced under the name “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TCFT"}> TCFT
            ”.
          %p
            The concept is essentially a formalization of what used to be called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+field+theory"} cohomological field theory
            in
          %ul
            %li#Witten91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to cohomological field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WittenCQFT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p The definition was given independently by
          %ul
            %li#Getzler92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ezra+Getzler"}> Ezra Getzler
              ,
              %em Batalin-Vilkovisky algebras and two-dimensional topological field theories
              , Comm. Math. Phys. 159(2), 265–285 (1994) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9212043"}> arXiv:hep-th/9212043
              )
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#Segal99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              %em Topological field theory
              , (1999), Notes of lectures at Stanford university. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.cgtp.duke.edu/ITP99/segal/"}> web
              ). See in particular
              %a{:href => "http://www.cgtp.duke.edu/ITP99/segal/stanford/lect5.pdf"} lecture 5
              (“topological field theory with cochain values”).
          %p
            The classification of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TCFT"} TCFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended
            D=2 TQFT)) by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+A-infinity+categories"} Calabi-Yau A-infinity categories
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Costello04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                ,
                %em Topological conformal field theories and Calabi-Yau categories
                Advances in Mathematics, Volume 210, Issue 1, (2007), (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0412149"}> arXiv:math/0412149
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                ,
                %em The Gromov-Witten potential associated to a TCFT
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0509264"}> arXiv:math/0509264
                )
          %p
            following conjectures by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
          %ul
            %li#Kontsevich95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              %em Homological algebra of mirror symmetry
              , in Proceedings of the International Congress of Mathematicians, Vol. 1, 2 (Zürich, 1994), pages 120–139, Basel, 1995, Birkhäuser.
          %p
            The classification of local (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"}> extended
            ) D=2 TQFT (i.e. the “compact” but fully local case) is spelled out in
          %ul
            %li#SchommerPries11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
              ,
              %em The Classification of Two-Dimensional Extended Topological Field Theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1112.1000"}> arXiv:1112.1000
              )
          %p
            This classification is a precursor of the full
            = succeed "-theorem." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
          %ul
            %li#Lurie09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 4.2 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.0465"}> arXiv:0905.0465
              )
